# "Listing_Custom_Fields_API/README.md"
# Listing Custom Fields API

This project provides a production-friendly implementation of an API endpoint inspired by OpenGever and Plone REST API integrations. It discovers property sheet definitions assigned to supported listings, filters fields to those that can be indexed in Solr, and returns a stable JSON structure for clients that render dynamic listing columns.

The core endpoint is compatible with the intent of GET /@listing-custom-fields:

- dossiers receive fields assigned to dossier property sheet slots
- documents receive fields assigned to document property sheet slots
- text-only fields are excluded because they are not suitable as Solr dynamic listing fields
- duplicate Solr dynamic field names are resolved by last assignment wins

## Quick start

Install the package in editable mode:

    python -m pip install -e .[test]

Create example data:

    listing-fields write-example --target ./var/propertysheets

Run the HTTP service:

    LISTING_FIELDS_SCHEMA_DIR=./var/propertysheets uvicorn listing_custom_fields.app:create_app --factory --reload

Fetch fields:

    curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/@listing-custom-fields

Use the CLI directly:

    listing-fields list --schema-dir ./var/propertysheets

Run tests:

    pytest

## Property sheet format

Definitions are JSON files with a slot name and field definitions. A slot binds a property sheet to a business context such as document_default or dossier_contracts. The API resolves configured slot providers and merges all matching fields into listing groups.

